Organizations may consider implementation of an all-in              -one solution for configuration
management. For example, various            configuration management  functions are included in
products for managing servers, workstations, desktops  , and services provided by applications .
The products may include functions such as:

           •                                        Inventory/discovery of system components;
           •                                        Software distribution;
           •                                       Patch management;
           •                                        Operating system deployment;
           •                                        Policy management;
           •                                        Migration to new baseline configuration; and
           •                                        Backup/recovery              .

