Determine Configuration Items
When implementing                                             configuration management, the system owner determines                                           how to best
decompose the system                               into one or more configuration items  (CIs).               CIs may be one or a group of
system components, documents, network diagrams, scripts, custom code, and various other
elements that compose the system and which require configuration management.

